From e31f940d8ac373e5d38453fb8dbec8cc0a7b6fd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vlad Syan <vlad.syan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:54:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(FlyView): RF direction-finding overlay and ArduPlane
 RFSearch mode

For a SITL demo with a companion that reports received RF power:
- RFScanMapItems.qml draws the nose antenna's beam coloured by RF_dBm,
  a fading trail and power dots, the companion's bearings (RF_BRG) with
  +-sigma wedges, source fixes as 1-sigma error ellipses (RF_FIX) and,
  in SITL, the true sources (RF_TRU) with their distance to the nearest fix;
- Vehicle parses the companion's NAMED_VALUE_FLOAT RF_dBm / RFS_SWP and
  DEBUG_FLOAT_ARRAY RF_BRG / RF_FIX / RF_TRU into signals and a new "rf"
  fact group (dBm, sweep phase, sweeps, bearings, sources);
- ArduPlaneFirmwarePlugin knows custom mode 27 "RFSearch".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
